text/html,96bb14c8cf57bcf1dd5d0736cb5078d9cc7c23e529d888d70b21de47763e35af,retained prior type,0,"﻿ PDF WAC 415-106-245 Are retroactive salary increases reportable compensation? A retroactive salary increase occurs when your rate of pay is increased and made retroactive to a prior date. You receive a lump sum payment to cover the increase earned during the earlier period. (1) To qualify as reportable compensation under this section, the retroactive salary increase must be made pursuant to: (a) An order or conciliation agreement of a court or administrative agency charged with enforcing federal, state, or local statutes, ordinances, or regulations protecting employment rights; (b) A bona fi","{""bounded_link_count"": 3, ""bounded_visible_character_count"": 1077, ""html_title"": """"}",1944,https://lawfilesext.leg.wa.gov/Law/WACArchive/2020/htm/WAC%20415%20%20TITLE/WAC%20415%20-106%20%20CHAPTER/WAC%20415%20-106%20-245.htm,EXTLOC-3c24c211018b0a5fb7218ac9,,unclear,html,200,payroll_roster,https://lawfilesext.leg.wa.gov/Law/WACArchive/2020/htm/WAC%20415%20%20TITLE/WAC%20415%20-106%20%20CHAPTER/WAC%20415%20-106%20-245.htm,high,0,0,False,RESCAND-9f3a5016f6e5f9c0ac9bf5b8,,MECHEXP-11bc678fccdfd3c029869852|MECHEXP-33162c8161292340bd895cd7|MECHEXP-3b30897255b1f9b64c76a966|MECHEXP-52f7f1b7743c4c1a4e21560d|MECHEXP-5b07257bb2b86260ad522462|MECHEXP-6507d9dd2c3e7c8bbb0871eb|MECHEXP-65be90245a8a4e734a461957|MECHEXP-67856a733785676ffeda03b3|MECHEXP-76dc7c73949a5eb2efb74ff8|MECHEXP-889364e73dc1ca117e3e50eb|MECHEXP-8933896c04c74c3f3dc51745|MECHEXP-caaee7e01596c697c83fcec2|MECHEXP-da7f2f68c8a3d62614ae74b5|MECHEXP-dbdb2dec35acc76c517beab3,ROOTCOMP-1270a740fa570d096bb60983|ROOTCOMP-31925e7a7b94d67d6bba46c3|ROOTCOMP-66773447e6a05796c9613a66,external_search_wave_002_exhaustive_residual,artifacts/local_retained_sources/whole_corpus_external_data_exhaustive_pipeline_2026-08-04/html/96bb14c8cf57bcf1dd5d0736cb5078d9cc7c23e529d888d70b21de47763e35af.html,lawfilesext.leg.wa.gov,Chuathbaluk,0,true,W